WEBVTT

00:00.560 --> 00:03.480
<i>The temperature out here is about 35°C.</i>

00:03.480 --> 00:07.060
<i>The players will have to fight hard in this sweltering heat.</i>

00:08.270 --> 00:13.070
<i>Since you're injured, a shot from this distance ought to be enough to crush you!</i>

00:14.200 --> 00:15.700
<i>He got it!</i>

00:15.700 --> 00:17.780
<i>Wakabayashi firmly catches the ball!</i>

00:17.780 --> 00:18.700
What?!

00:19.530 --> 00:25.660
<i>Hyuga, even if my leg breaks, I won't concede another goal to you!</i>

00:25.660 --> 00:26.830
Damn it!

00:27.240 --> 00:28.040
Here!

00:28.580 --> 00:31.270
<i>Wakabayashi kicks the ball far away.</i>

00:31.270 --> 00:34.080
<i>The first half has started with a long shot from Hyuga.</i>

00:34.080 --> 00:38.050
<i>That's right! The extra time begins now!</i>

00:50.090 --> 00:55.700
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

00:50.090 --> 00:55.700
<i>koronda toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

00:55.700 --> 01:00.750
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

00:55.700 --> 01:00.750
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

01:01.420 --> 01:06.550
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

01:01.420 --> 01:06.550
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

01:07.300 --> 01:14.890
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

01:07.300 --> 01:14.890
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

01:14.890 --> 01:20.660
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

01:14.890 --> 01:20.660
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

01:20.660 --> 01:29.160
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

01:20.660 --> 01:29.160
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

01:29.160 --> 01:34.950
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

01:29.160 --> 01:34.950
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

01:34.950 --> 01:40.880
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

01:34.950 --> 01:40.880
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

01:40.880 --> 01:42.420
<i>Run & Run!</i>

01:42.420 --> 01:49.710
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

01:42.420 --> 01:49.710
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

01:49.710 --> 01:52.630
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Let's go, it's kickoff!</i>

01:49.710 --> 01:52.630
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kickoff</i>

01:52.630 --> 01:57.560
<i>Leap out into a giant field of dreams</i>

01:52.630 --> 01:57.560
<i>tobidasô dodekai dream field</i>

02:08.270 --> 02:13.150
<b><b>EPISODE 26:
PHANTOM GOAL</b></b>

02:09.060 --> 02:13.440
<i>Nankatsu's captain, Tsubasa Ozora, dribbles into Meiwa's side of the field.</i>

02:13.440 --> 02:15.190
Go! Steal it back from him!

02:15.840 --> 02:17.780
<i>Listen to me, Tsubasa.</i>

02:17.780 --> 02:20.360
<i>I'll support your injured left leg with bandages.</i>

02:20.360 --> 02:23.070
<i>If I do that, you won't feel much pain.</i>

02:23.070 --> 02:25.870
<i>So, run and kick the ball to your heart's content.</i>

02:26.420 --> 02:32.020
<i>But I'll be using more tape on your ankle, so it'll be hard to control the ball with your left leg.</i>

02:32.020 --> 02:32.920
<i>Okay.</i>

02:32.920 --> 02:33.670
Take this!

02:35.130 --> 02:37.800
<i>Meiwa's sliding squad attacks!</i>

02:39.550 --> 02:40.300
What?!

02:40.300 --> 02:45.220
<i>Tsubasa skillfully controls the ball with
his right leg, foregoing his injured left!</i>

02:45.220 --> 02:47.140
<i>That's very skillful footwork!</i>

02:47.140 --> 02:48.050
Awesome!

02:48.050 --> 02:49.640
You're doing great, Tsubasa!

02:50.640 --> 02:51.260
Here!

02:51.260 --> 02:51.870
What?!

02:51.870 --> 02:53.690
<i>Tsubasa takes a shot!</i>

02:53.690 --> 02:55.520
<i>I won't let you score!</i>

02:56.820 --> 03:01.200
<i>It seems it was more of a pass for Misaki, disguised as a shot!</i>

03:01.200 --> 03:03.780
<i>Misaki launches into a diving header!</i>

03:03.780 --> 03:04.580
We did it!

03:04.580 --> 03:06.370
We tricked Meiwa again!

03:07.960 --> 03:10.330
<i>Wakashimazu stops him!</i>

03:10.330 --> 03:11.330
What?

03:13.870 --> 03:15.460
Well, that was close!

03:16.090 --> 03:17.570
<i>Did he read into my moves?</i>

03:18.460 --> 03:20.320
<i>That's Wakashimazu for you.</i>

03:20.320 --> 03:23.430
<i>He won't repeat the same mistake again.</i>

03:24.430 --> 03:27.700
His name was Wakashimazu, right?

03:27.700 --> 03:30.560
Yes. Ken Wakashimazu.

03:30.560 --> 03:32.310
He's pretty good.

03:32.310 --> 03:33.770
Hyuga!

03:33.770 --> 03:35.020
This time...

03:35.020 --> 03:37.110
I'll score a goal!

03:37.110 --> 03:38.020
Wakabayashi!

03:43.650 --> 03:44.660
Damn it!

03:44.660 --> 03:46.410
Nice, Wakabayashi!

03:46.410 --> 03:48.120
Go!

03:48.120 --> 03:52.350
Both Wakabayashi and Wakashimazu are both doing really well.

03:52.350 --> 03:56.630
Who will score first in the extra time?

03:56.630 --> 04:00.590
They are all attacking, but defense has really become the key of the match.

04:00.590 --> 04:02.510
Here, to the goal!

04:02.510 --> 04:03.840
<i>Tsubasa...</i>

04:05.130 --> 04:06.430
<i>Misaki!</i>

04:06.430 --> 04:08.710
<i>The ball reaches Tsubasa!</i>

04:08.710 --> 04:10.930
<i>Tsubasa fires a jumping volley!</i>

04:24.680 --> 04:25.650
<i>And there he goes!</i>

04:25.650 --> 04:29.080
<i>An absolutely stunning save from Wakashimazu!</i>

04:29.080 --> 04:31.200
What the hell was that?

04:31.200 --> 04:32.450
Damn it...

04:34.330 --> 04:36.640
This has become quite the match.

04:36.640 --> 04:38.700
It's so hot, I think I'm going to pass out...

04:38.700 --> 04:41.380
They are all awesome. Truly awesome!

04:41.380 --> 04:44.050
Yeah, awesome...

04:44.050 --> 04:47.220
<i>Both teams must be feeling exhausted, but they've been going at it,</i>

04:47.220 --> 04:49.850
<i>trying to take the ball since the start of extra time.</i>

04:53.770 --> 04:56.150
<i>What's wrong with Misaki?</i>

04:56.150 --> 04:59.270
<i>He's holding his leg and kneeling down!</i>

05:00.020 --> 05:01.770
<i>Misaki can't move!</i>

05:01.770 --> 05:03.360
<i>All right, that's a chance for us!</i>

05:03.360 --> 05:04.570
Eat this!

05:04.570 --> 05:06.820
<i>Damn... Alright, come at me, then!</i>

05:06.820 --> 05:11.530
<i>If you all gather around me, Tsubasa will be freed up!</i>

05:11.530 --> 05:12.540
Misaki!

05:13.290 --> 05:16.500
<i>Misaki times a perfect pass forward!</i>

05:20.840 --> 05:21.590
Misaki!

05:24.460 --> 05:28.220
<i>He went as far as sacrificing his own leg,
just to send this pass to me...!</i>

05:29.580 --> 05:32.140
<i>I'll score this one, Misaki!</i>

05:34.310 --> 05:36.760
<i>Tsubasa tries his signature move for the third time!</i>

05:36.760 --> 05:38.810
<i>Here comes another overhead kick!</i>

05:38.810 --> 05:41.690
Eat this, Wakashimazu!

05:41.690 --> 05:42.940
Go!

05:44.900 --> 05:46.190
Stop him!

05:46.940 --> 05:49.070
I don't care how strong your shots are!

05:49.070 --> 05:51.570
You can't defeat me with long shots!

05:52.620 --> 05:53.580
What?!

05:54.140 --> 06:00.580
<i>He reached for Tsubasa's shot, but Wakashimazu just wasn't able to catch this one!</i>

06:04.090 --> 06:08.220
<i>It might've been that Tsubasa's overhead kick gave a lot of rotational force to the ball,</i>

06:08.220 --> 06:13.740
<i>but the ball Wakashimazu seemed to have barely saved, rebounded and ended up falling into the goal, instead!</i>

06:13.740 --> 06:18.240
<i>Moreover, the referee blew his whistle to mark the end of the first half at the same time!</i>

06:18.240 --> 06:20.520
<i>Will this goal be acknowledged?</i>

06:20.520 --> 06:21.520
Mr. Referee!

06:21.520 --> 06:23.770
Does this goal count or not?

06:27.490 --> 06:28.860
No goal!

06:30.490 --> 06:32.110
What do you mean, "no goal"?!

06:35.400 --> 06:37.160
Are you serious?

06:37.160 --> 06:40.390
<i>The referee decided that goal didn't count!</i>

06:40.390 --> 06:43.960
<i>The first half ends with a no-goal call!</i>

06:44.640 --> 06:46.130
Damn it all!

06:48.800 --> 06:49.760
Misaki!

06:49.760 --> 06:50.520
Are you OK?

06:50.520 --> 06:51.640
Misaki!

06:51.640 --> 06:54.140
I'm fine. I can play in the second half.

06:54.140 --> 06:55.680
Hold on to me!

06:57.400 --> 06:59.810
I'm sorry, I couldn't score.

06:59.810 --> 07:01.810
It's all right.

07:01.810 --> 07:03.940
Misaki...

07:15.640 --> 07:18.600
The team who scores in the next 5 minutes will win.

07:18.600 --> 07:19.700
Yeah.

07:19.700 --> 07:24.790
If we think about it, the goalkeepers aren't as tired as the other players. It'll come down to a single goal.

07:24.790 --> 07:28.570
Well, do you really think this match will be over once one of them scores?

07:28.570 --> 07:29.700
Of course it will!

07:29.700 --> 07:34.000
Neither team has the strength to play any more than 5 minutes.

07:34.000 --> 07:38.100
That's why they'll make their last desperate efforts in the second half.

07:38.100 --> 07:41.850
I can't predict who will win this match at all.

07:41.850 --> 07:42.810
Me either.

07:42.810 --> 07:46.770
<i>The second half of extra time is about to begin!</i>

07:46.770 --> 07:48.770
Good luck, Taro.

07:48.770 --> 07:51.030
<i>You made a promise, Misaki.</i>

07:51.030 --> 07:56.170
<i>When you feel like you can't play anymore,
when you're at your limit,</i>

07:56.170 --> 07:59.030
<i>you will take yourself out of the game.</i>

08:03.040 --> 08:08.800
Tsubasa, the first time I played with you
was also an extra time, wasn't it?

08:08.800 --> 08:11.420
Yes, it sure was.

08:14.050 --> 08:16.710
<i>Let's do this, Kojiro Hyuga!</i>

08:19.060 --> 08:24.060
player card

08:24.980 --> 08:28.110
<i>The second half of extra time finally begins!</i>

08:28.560 --> 08:31.780
<i>Nankatsu's captain Tsubasa charges into Meiwa's side of the field.</i>

08:31.780 --> 08:33.320
We will stop him this time!

08:33.320 --> 08:34.150
Yeah!

08:34.150 --> 08:37.120
We will work hard in Misaki's stead this time!

08:37.120 --> 08:37.910
Yeah!

08:37.910 --> 08:42.660
<i>Under the gaze of the huge crowd, time is ticking away!</i>

08:42.660 --> 08:48.670
<i>In this fierce derby, Meiwa vs Nankatsu...
which side will lady luck smile upon today?</i>

08:48.670 --> 08:51.420
<i>It is impossible to predict who will win.</i>

08:52.130 --> 08:54.920
<i>Tsubasa battles his way through!</i>

08:54.920 --> 08:57.090
<i>With both sides having issues scoring,</i>

08:57.090 --> 09:00.300
<i>Tsubasa lets loose a long shot with all of his might!</i>

09:00.880 --> 09:03.380
<i>Wakashimazu makes the catch!</i>

09:03.380 --> 09:04.420
Captain!

09:04.420 --> 09:07.310
You're the only one in Meiwa who can score, now!

09:07.310 --> 09:08.580
All right!

09:09.480 --> 09:10.380
Big bro!

09:10.380 --> 09:11.610
Good luck!

09:11.610 --> 09:14.740
<i>This time, Hyuga is the one charging into enemy territory!</i>

09:14.740 --> 09:16.030
Damn!

09:16.670 --> 09:18.820
<i>Hyuga takes a long shot as well!</i>

09:19.530 --> 09:23.950
<i>But Nankatsu's keeper Wakabayashi won't let a goal past so easily!</i>

09:23.950 --> 09:24.780
Damn you!

09:24.780 --> 09:27.370
<i>Even the two aces who have scored every goal this match</i>

09:27.370 --> 09:30.250
<i>are unable to hide the mounting fatigue from their faces.</i>

09:30.250 --> 09:34.170
It seems that both keepers' stamina is mostly intact.

09:34.170 --> 09:36.670
<i>The ball is once again with Tsubasa.</i>

09:36.670 --> 09:37.650
<i>Brazil...</i>

09:37.650 --> 09:39.800
<i>I will win and go to Brazil with Roberto</i>,

09:39.800 --> 09:42.810
<i>to the country of football!</i>

09:42.810 --> 09:47.230
<i>I will be the number one footballer in the world.</i>

09:47.230 --> 09:48.960
<i>Like I'd lose!</i>

09:48.960 --> 09:51.230
<i>I will win and join Toho Academy,</i>

09:51.230 --> 09:55.740
<i>and make my family happy through my own efforts!</i>

10:00.160 --> 10:04.160
<i>Tsubasa and Hyuga are fighting for the ball again!</i>

10:05.160 --> 10:09.670
Damn, I really need to cover Tsubasa at a time like this, but...

10:09.670 --> 10:13.420
Damn it, I will save Hyuga!

10:13.420 --> 10:15.920
<i>We are in the climax of the grand finals!</i>

10:15.920 --> 10:20.680
<i>Will it be Meiwa or Nankatsu that will earn this last chance for victory?</i>

10:20.680 --> 10:22.340
Do your best, Tsubasa!

10:22.340 --> 10:24.340
Don't yield the ball to Hyuga!

10:30.060 --> 10:31.350
I've got to save Tsu–

10:32.730 --> 10:33.900
My leg...

10:33.900 --> 10:35.360
Hyuga!

10:36.110 --> 10:37.420
Okay!

10:37.420 --> 10:41.360
<i>Hyuga takes the ball, taking advantage of a moment of carelessness.</i>

10:42.680 --> 10:44.030
Damn!

10:49.460 --> 10:50.620
Tsubasa...

10:55.020 --> 10:58.200
<i>Both of them fall to the ground, all tangled up with each other!</i>

10:58.200 --> 11:00.260
<i>The ball crosses over the sideline!</i>

11:01.370 --> 11:05.390
Keep fighting, big bro! You're almost there!

11:05.390 --> 11:07.390
You guys...

11:08.890 --> 11:09.920
The ball is Meiwa's!

11:09.920 --> 11:10.980
Hyuga!

11:10.980 --> 11:12.090
Takeshi.

11:14.980 --> 11:16.020
Tsubasa.

11:16.020 --> 11:17.190
Hyuga!

11:21.200 --> 11:23.700
TSUBASA PULLS A NEYMAR

11:24.500 --> 11:27.700
<i>Has Tsubasa finally run out of stamina?!</i>

11:27.700 --> 11:28.540
Tsubasa!

11:28.540 --> 11:31.410
<i>It looks like the last chance will go to Meiwa!</i>

11:31.410 --> 11:33.210
Big bro!

11:33.210 --> 11:34.710
Just watch me, guys!

11:34.710 --> 11:37.720
I will put an end to this match!

11:37.720 --> 11:39.810
As if we'd let you do that!

11:39.810 --> 11:42.590
Let's put our bodies on the line and stop his advance!

11:42.590 --> 11:43.720
Yeah!

11:54.520 --> 11:55.480
Hyuga...!

11:55.480 --> 11:57.070
<i>He feints and dribbles through!</i>

11:57.070 --> 12:00.990
<i>Hyuga has thrown his pride away, aiming for victory!</i>

12:00.990 --> 12:03.990
That guy had such strength left?!

12:06.350 --> 12:09.030
<i>Oh, Hyuga slips and loses his balance!</i>

12:09.030 --> 12:10.700
This is my chance!

12:11.950 --> 12:14.120
You did it, Ishizaki!

12:16.290 --> 12:18.540
It's not over yet, Hyuga!

12:18.540 --> 12:23.940
This truly is the last pass I can give you!

12:24.800 --> 12:25.910
Takeshi!

12:25.910 --> 12:28.800
<i>The ball is high, right above Hyuga!</i>

12:28.800 --> 12:32.280
<i>Takeshi, I made a promise to you, didn't I?</i>

12:32.280 --> 12:34.460
<i>That we would win together!</i>

12:34.460 --> 12:35.550
<i>That's right.</i>

12:35.550 --> 12:37.560
<i>So long as you pass the ball to me,</i>

12:37.560 --> 12:39.560
<i>I will definitely take the shot!</i>

12:43.070 --> 12:50.330
<i>Hyuga goes for the championship with an overhead kick!</i>

12:50.330 --> 12:54.890
<i>If I let him score now, what would've been
the meaning of my coming here?</i>

12:54.890 --> 12:58.790
<i>What would their hard work have amounted to?!</i>

12:58.790 --> 13:00.320
Eat this, Wakabayashi!

13:00.320 --> 13:03.260
We will be the winners!

13:06.340 --> 13:09.180
<i>He caught it!</i>

13:09.180 --> 13:10.260
Genzo!

13:14.200 --> 13:16.270
I protected the goal, guys!

13:16.270 --> 13:17.900
Wakabayashi!

13:19.140 --> 13:23.830
<i>There goes the whistle, signaling the end of this extra time!</i>

13:23.830 --> 13:26.150
<i>We are going into an additional extra time!</i>

13:26.150 --> 13:29.050
<i>The National Youth Football Tournament grand finals,</i>

13:29.050 --> 13:32.920
<i>Nankatsu vs Meiwa, has yet to come to a conclusion at the end of the first extra time!</i>

13:32.920 --> 13:36.230
<i>The match will proceed into an additional extra time.</i>

13:36.230 --> 13:40.330
<i>If. after this, a winner has yet to be decided,
there will be no more extra time.</i>

13:40.330 --> 13:42.040
<i>No penalty shootouts, either.</i>

13:42.040 --> 13:44.800
<i>Both teams will be declared as co-champions.</i>

13:45.380 --> 13:47.300
The players are exhausted as hell.

13:47.300 --> 13:49.960
They should just declare both sides as co-champions.

13:52.810 --> 13:55.390
"That was a good match."

13:55.390 --> 13:57.310
Taro...

13:57.310 --> 14:01.960
If both teams are declared as winners, which one will you choose

14:01.960 --> 14:03.690
between Hyuga and Tsubasa?

14:05.960 --> 14:09.360
Don't worry, I've already made my decision.

14:13.120 --> 14:17.250
<i>It's about time for the final match to be over, isn't it Tsubasa?</i>

14:17.250 --> 14:20.880
<i>Your dad believes in your victory.</i>

14:20.880 --> 14:26.630
<i>Your happy face as the winner will be there,</i>

14:26.630 --> 14:33.260
<i>just on the other side of the vivid rainbow made by passing rain, in Japan.</i>

14:45.090 --> 14:46.530
It's raining!

14:48.030 --> 14:49.150
It's raining!

14:49.150 --> 14:50.700
Rain...

15:09.760 --> 15:12.060
That was some good rain.

15:12.060 --> 15:12.760
Yeah.

15:12.760 --> 15:16.260
Now I've gathered enough strength to put an end to this match.

15:16.260 --> 15:20.180
We didn't get more extra time in the inter-school tournament, you know,

15:20.180 --> 15:23.120
so our duel never had a conclusion, Tsubasa.

15:23.990 --> 15:26.110
If that tournament had more extra time,

15:26.110 --> 15:29.530
I'm sure Nankatsu would've won it!

15:29.530 --> 15:31.420
What are you on about now, Ishizaki?

15:31.420 --> 15:35.200
You couldn't even keep playing after hurting your leg!

15:35.200 --> 15:36.960
That did happen, didn't it?

15:36.960 --> 15:40.040
Kishida and I argued that one of us should get to play

15:40.040 --> 15:41.620
and replace Ishizaki.

15:41.620 --> 15:44.460
Misaki wound up playing in the end, though!

15:44.460 --> 15:48.210
Tsubasa and Misaki's Golden Duo started back then.

15:48.210 --> 15:51.680
Guys, you need to hold out and work for another 10 minutes.

15:51.680 --> 15:54.470
If this also ends in a tie, both teams will be champions.

15:54.470 --> 15:57.140
That's not an option for us, coach.

15:57.140 --> 15:58.180
Tsubasa...

15:58.180 --> 16:01.150
We lost to Meiwa in the first match.

16:01.150 --> 16:03.690
So now, we must win this match!

16:03.690 --> 16:06.690
Otherwise, we have no right to call ourselves true champions.

16:12.860 --> 16:14.200
We must attack.

16:14.200 --> 16:15.700
Eh?

16:15.700 --> 16:19.190
Playing to win is Meiwa's style.

16:19.190 --> 16:21.340
We aren't aiming to get a tie.

16:21.340 --> 16:23.740
That's why attacking is our only choice.

16:23.740 --> 16:25.330
Isn't that right, coach?

16:25.330 --> 16:28.920
Yeah. There's only one championship pennant, as the name suggests.

16:28.920 --> 16:32.590
Meiwa should take it home, no matter what.

16:32.590 --> 16:38.160
The gods of football must've brought the rain to let everyone relax.

16:38.160 --> 16:40.390
I'd like to believe that too.

16:41.220 --> 16:42.680
Tsubasa!

16:42.680 --> 16:49.150
I feel like if I keep on playing, I'll be a burden to you all.

16:49.150 --> 16:52.120
Is your leg in a lot of pain?

16:52.120 --> 16:54.220
My leg's okay.

16:54.220 --> 16:57.410
Even if my leg were to break,
I want to keep playing with you all,

16:57.410 --> 17:00.330
But with the way I'm playing right now, I'll just—

17:00.330 --> 17:01.910
What are you going on about?

17:01.910 --> 17:07.500
There's no way I can get a ball past
Wakashimazu if you aren't here, Misaki!

17:07.500 --> 17:08.380
But...

17:08.380 --> 17:15.930
He's right. Only Nankatsu's Golden Duo, Tsubasa and Misaki, can score a goal against Wakashimazu now.

17:15.930 --> 17:17.800
I have a suggestion for that.

17:17.800 --> 17:20.070
We should let Meiwa attack in the first half.

17:20.070 --> 17:20.850
What?

17:20.850 --> 17:23.420
I want you two to rest.

17:23.420 --> 17:24.860
Wakabayashi...

17:24.860 --> 17:27.730
In their stead, you guys all should defend our side.

17:27.730 --> 17:31.730
We must do everything we can to stop Meiwa from scoring.

17:31.730 --> 17:34.610
And we'll bet on Tsubasa and Misaki in the second half.

17:34.610 --> 17:38.490
All right! I can't think of a better plan to beat Meiwa.

17:39.170 --> 17:40.780
Let's do it, Misaki.

17:40.780 --> 17:43.410
Okay. I'll use my final strength.

17:45.370 --> 17:48.870
<i>These 10 minutes are really the final minutes of this match.</i>

17:48.870 --> 17:53.350
<i>The first half of the additional extra time starts with Meiwa's kick-off.</i>

17:53.350 --> 17:54.710
All right! We go and attack!

17:54.710 --> 17:56.060
Okay!

17:57.050 --> 18:00.050
Guys! We'll give it our all to protect here!

18:01.920 --> 18:03.100
Here I go!

18:05.180 --> 18:07.180
Don't leave Hyuga open!

18:08.270 --> 18:09.810
He'll be passing it to Hyuga!

18:09.810 --> 18:11.010
Mark him!

18:12.690 --> 18:13.940
Hyuga!

18:13.940 --> 18:18.610
<i>Excellent pass work between Sawada and Hyuga, as if threading the needle!</i>

18:18.610 --> 18:19.490
We'll stop them!

18:19.490 --> 18:20.360
Right!

18:24.370 --> 18:25.680
Damn!

18:28.750 --> 18:30.250
That was cool, Wakabayashi!

18:32.080 --> 18:34.420
<i>Hyuga tries to break through the middle!</i>

18:39.930 --> 18:41.100
Damn it!

18:42.420 --> 18:45.140
<i>Will these two be unable to stop Hyuga?</i>

18:46.740 --> 18:47.890
What?!

18:47.890 --> 18:49.820
How many more times did you think you'd do this?!

18:49.820 --> 18:52.900
We are Nankatsu's defenders!

18:58.140 --> 19:00.280
<i>The defenders of Nankatsu did it!</i>

19:00.280 --> 19:03.200
<i>They've stopped Hyuga's attempt at breaking through!</i>

19:03.200 --> 19:05.090
Nice, Takasugi!

19:06.400 --> 19:08.700
Be careful! Mark Tsubasa and Misaki!

19:08.700 --> 19:09.710
On it!

19:10.830 --> 19:11.830
Urabe!

19:12.770 --> 19:14.210
Wait, did he trick me?!

19:14.210 --> 19:15.340
Izawa!

19:17.430 --> 19:21.180
<i>Nankatsu's attack is mostly just circulating the ball!</i>

19:21.870 --> 19:25.550
<i>Meanwhile, Tsubasa and Misaki aren't on the attack!</i>

19:25.550 --> 19:28.950
Why aren't Tsubasa and Misaki moving?

19:28.950 --> 19:31.240
That must be Nankatsu's plan.

19:31.240 --> 19:34.310
There's no doubt that they'll risk it all in the second half.

19:34.310 --> 19:37.980
<i>Nankatsu's defense is as tight-knit as ever!</i>

19:37.980 --> 19:41.490
<i>They completely mark Meiwa's ace Hyuga and Sawada,</i>

19:41.490 --> 19:44.740
<i>and they prevent the others from shooting!</i>

19:44.740 --> 19:47.490
<i>Even then, Meiwa obstinately keeps shooting,</i>

19:47.490 --> 19:51.290
<i>only to see the few shots they can muster stopped by Wakabayashi!</i>

19:51.290 --> 19:53.040
This bastard...

19:53.040 --> 19:56.170
<i>Wakabayashi is like a guardian angel!</i>

19:57.550 --> 20:01.340
My leg is close to its limit, too.

20:01.340 --> 20:04.970
There's just a minute left. We should hold out somehow!

20:04.970 --> 20:06.350
Yeah.

20:06.350 --> 20:10.040
<i>Nankatsu won't attack at all in this first half.</i>

20:10.040 --> 20:12.890
<i>Tsubasa and Misaki haven't even moved at all.</i>

20:12.890 --> 20:16.280
<i>Are their injuries that bad?</i>

20:16.280 --> 20:17.900
<i>Could it be they—</i>

20:17.900 --> 20:22.150
Captain! Nankatsu has been on defense on purpose in the first half!

20:22.150 --> 20:23.150
What?

20:23.150 --> 20:27.780
They intend to let Tsubasa and Misaki rest, and make them come at us in the second half!

20:27.780 --> 20:29.160
So he saw through it...

20:29.160 --> 20:30.550
It's exactly what you think!

20:30.550 --> 20:32.380
There's only 30 seconds left.

20:32.380 --> 20:35.170
We'll just keep defending, Hyuga!

20:35.170 --> 20:38.300
<i>I don't care about your cheap tricks!</i>

20:38.300 --> 20:42.000
<i>We'll just keep attacking in this first half and the next!</i>

20:42.000 --> 20:46.130
<i>We'll attack, attack and keep on attacking,
and then we'll seize victory!</i>

20:46.820 --> 20:48.420
Let's do this, Wakabayashi!

20:48.420 --> 20:50.140
<i>Hyuga breaks through the middle!</i>

20:50.140 --> 20:52.140
Stop him! Stop him from shooting!

20:52.140 --> 20:55.990
<i>We'll stop him. We must prevent Meiwa from scoring this half!</i>

20:55.990 --> 21:01.530
<i>If we don't, all of our planning will have been for nothing!</i>

21:01.530 --> 21:02.530
Wakabayashi!

21:04.640 --> 21:06.660
<i>Hyuga won't fire a shot!</i>

21:07.170 --> 21:11.910
<i>Incredible! The keeper Wakashimazu is running towards the goal!</i>

21:11.910 --> 21:13.640
<i>Go, Wakashimazu!</i>

21:13.640 --> 21:16.630
<i>You still have plenty of strength left!</i>

21:16.630 --> 21:20.420
<i>And your powerful kicks rival mine!</i>

21:23.170 --> 21:24.170
Wakabayashi!

21:24.170 --> 21:25.930
<i>So that was it, Wakashimazu!</i>

21:25.930 --> 21:29.430
<i>If it were me aiming for a goal, I'd shoot here too!</i>

21:30.660 --> 21:32.350
<i>He got it!</i>

21:32.350 --> 21:33.060
What?!

21:34.580 --> 21:36.060
Wakabayashi...

21:36.060 --> 21:39.400
<i>Wakabayashi manages to make a brilliant save here!</i>

21:39.400 --> 21:43.320
<i>And the whistle marks the end of the first half of the additional extra time.</i>

21:44.570 --> 21:46.540
You did it, Wakabayashi!

21:46.540 --> 21:48.320
We successfully defended this half!

21:49.860 --> 21:55.830
<i>You aimed for the hardest spot for a keeper, the lower left corner of the goal.</i>

21:55.830 --> 21:59.830
<i>It takes one goalkeeper to know another one.</i>

21:59.830 --> 22:02.240
<i>Tsubasa, Misaki...</i>

22:02.240 --> 22:04.340
<i>We didn't let them score in the first half.</i>

22:04.340 --> 22:08.010
<i>It's the Golden Duo's turn in the second half.</i>

22:08.010 --> 22:13.890
Misaki, Wakabayashi and the others
kept the score even, as promised.

22:14.610 --> 22:16.330
Now, it's our turn.

22:16.330 --> 22:17.420
Right!

22:20.020 --> 23:50.030
I want drunk Hyuga back

22:38.750 --> 22:44.630
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.750 --> 22:44.630
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.630 --> 22:50.630
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.630 --> 22:50.630
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.630 --> 22:56.640
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.630 --> 22:56.640
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.640 --> 23:02.100
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.640 --> 23:02.100
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.060 --> 23:08.240
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.060 --> 23:08.240
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.150 --> 23:14.950
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.150 --> 23:14.950
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:14.950 --> 23:21.000
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.000 --> 23:26.000
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.000 --> 23:26.000
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.300 --> 23:33.180
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.300 --> 23:33.180
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.180 --> 23:39.060
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.060 --> 23:45.940
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.060 --> 23:45.940
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.030 --> 24:00.640
COMING UP, EPISODE 27:
THE MOMENT OF GLORY
